  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Thanks for digging into this, the double count looks like the right cause. I tried it on 2 GPUs with ZeRO-3 and a plain use_reentrant=True checkpoint, no module reused, and it fails on the first step with AttributeError: 'Linear' object has no attribute 'ds_grads_remaining', raised from the post backward function. Master runs that fine. I think the graph task id check skips the recompute's setup, so the counter never gets created, which is what the codex comment was getting at. Also, without the reset, a module that is called but whose output never reaches the loss keeps its count at +1, and it grew by one every step in my run (1, 2, 3, 4), so the release stops firing. yapf fails on the new condition line and the commit needs a Signed-off-by.\n",
